  "hypothesis": "Aligning point coordinate arrays to 16-byte boundaries via posix_memalign in parse_next_group, hoisting invariant NEON vector constants (tx_vec, ty_vec) outside the group loop, adding restrict qualifiers with __builtin_assume_aligned hints inside knn, prefetching upcoming cache lines, and using bit shifts for heap index calculations reduce memory latency and instruction count while preserving legal SIMD/vectorization. These changes further improve runtime over the SoA+NEON implementation.",
